  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nOverall, hot and dry conditions remain in place due to strong\nridging over northeast Montana through early this weekend. A\ncouple of small shortwaves are moving through the region through\nThursday, leading to periodic rain chances which will be in\nisolated to scattered form. Yet this afternoon, there remains\nchances for severe thunderstorms along the North Dakota border\nwith severe winds being the main threat. The current pattern \nculminates in potentially the hottest day of the year on Saturday,\nwhere widespread 100s to 110s will be likely. \n\nA dry cold front moves through Saturday night, which will lead to\na slow pattern change, and relief from the heat for many. Sunday\nwill be highlighted by critical concerns for fire weather while\nremaining hot, but windy. By Monday, afternoon high temperatures \nacross the region could be in the 70s and 80s, which would be a \n20-30 degree cooldown from Saturday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nHigh confidence in the hot weather continuing through Saturday.\nConfidence is increasing rapidly on major concerns for critical\nfire weather on Sunday. Low confidence in timing any showers and \nthunderstorms.\n\nNo major deviations from the base forecast were made for this\niteration.\n\nCliff",
